I see that DotIgnoreIgnoreRule is a concrete class with a public parameterless constructor, so I can instantiate it directly in the test without mocking.

I also need to fix the mocking of IHostApplicationLifetime.ApplicationStarted and ApplicationStopping properties. They are of type CancellationToken, so I should mock them as CancellationToken properties.

I will rewrite the test to instantiate DotIgnoreIgnoreRule directly and mock IHostApplicationLifetime.ApplicationStarted and ApplicationStopping as CancellationToken properties.

I will submit the corrected test now.

